#include <turnkey/base>

/* The web half is the parent layer, apache-php, and fab-plan-resolve keeps a
   package the parent already carries at the parent's version, so nothing the
   parent installs is named again here: apache2, libapache2-mod-php, php-cli,
   libapache2-mod-security2, libapache2-mod-evasive, libapache2-mod-perl2,
   webmin-apache, webmin-phpini, adminer, libjs-jush and composer.

   The database server, python3-pymysql and webmin-mysql are the plan of the
   unit.d/mariadb component, which fab resolves together with this one when
   the unit is present. They are not named here, and that is what makes the
   second artefact of this recipe an image with no server: remove the unit and
   the three packages go with it, rather than being left behind by a name in
   this file. */

/* The four packages that make this stack MariaDB's rather than another
   engine's. LAPP names the same four roles with the PostgreSQL packages and
   nothing else differs, which is the point of decision 0013's layer model.

   Each is needed in both artefacts: the client and the drivers are how the
   stack reaches a database, and where that database lives is a setting, not
   a package. */
mariadb-client           /* the command line client */
php-mysql                /* the PHP driver, which is what the stack runs on */
libdbd-mysql-perl        /* the Perl DBI driver, for mod_perl2 from the parent */
python3-mysqldb          /* the Python driver */

/* project packages, resolved from the build host's staging repository: the
   declarative first boot that turns secrets.db_password into DB_PASS lives in
   inithooks, the console screens in confconsole, and keel is the instance
   description tool the appliance answers keel inspect with. core carries the
   stock inithooks and confconsole and no keel at all, so conf.d/main upgrades
   the two and checks the floor. */
inithooks
confconsole
keel

/* Deliberately not here, and each for its own reason, all four named in the
   changelog because dropping a package upstream ships is a content decision:

   libapache2-mod-python  gone from Debian 13, and gone upstream long before
                          that; mod_python has no maintained release for
                          Apache 2.4.
   php-xdebug             a step debugger and profiler. It belongs on a
                          developer's machine and not switched on in a
                          published appliance, where it costs performance and
                          reports internals to whoever can reach a page.
   php-pear               superseded by composer, which the parent already
                          carries, and which both stacks use.
   python3-pygresql       LAPP's second Python driver. One driver per language
                          per stack, so this stack names python3-mysqldb and
                          LAPP names python3-psycopg2.

   The first three are upstream LAMP's and have no LAPP counterpart; the
   fourth is upstream LAPP's and has no LAMP counterpart. Keeping them would
   make the two recipes differ in something other than the database, which is
   the one thing the composition is being measured on. */
